    "result_text": "Done. The change is complete and the test suite is green (`Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 `BUILD SUCCESS`).\n\n## What I changed\n\n**`memberId` format** \u2014 `<REGION><FY><HASH8><CHK>` concatenated with no separators, e.g. the created owner got `NSW2616E6609E3` (region `NSW`, fiscal year `26`, HASH8 `16E6609E`, Luhn check `3`).\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 Replaced the `customerCode`, `checkDigit`, and `membershipNumber` schema properties with a single `memberId` property; updated the `locality` description to reference the memberId's region prefix. (The generated `OwnerDto` + MapStruct pick up `memberId` automatically from `Owner.getMemberId()`.)\n\n2. **`Owner.java`**\n   - Replaced the persisted `customerCode` field/accessors with `memberId` (`member_id` column).\n   - Removed `getCheckDigit()` and `getMembershipNumber()`.\n   - `getFiscalYear()` now reads the FY segment out of the memberId; `getLocality()` reads the region prefix out of the memberId (so `ownerSegment`/`timezone` reference it) \u2014 both stripping any `-<n>` collision suffix via a shared `memberIdBase()` helper.\n\n3. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`**\n   - `memberIdFor(owner)` builds `REGION + FY + HASH8`, computes the Luhn CHK over that, and appends it; `deduplicateMemberId(...)` applies collision handling to the memberId.\n   - Audit updated: flat log line now emits `memberId=\u2026`, and `primaryIdentifier`/`ownerCreatedEvent` carry the memberId (JSON key renamed to `memberId`).\n   - Added `fiscalYearStart(...)` and `luhnCheckDigit(...)` helpers; reused the existing SHA-256 `telephoneNameHash` so HASH8 matches the region-and-hash identity.\n\n4. **`db/{hsqldb,mysql,h2,postgres}/schema.sql`** \u2014 Renamed `customer_code` \u2192 `member_id` and widened it to `VARCHAR(32)` (an `UNKNOWN` region plus a collision suffix can exceed the old 20 chars). The test profile (`hsqldb`, `ddl-auto=none`) relies on this schema.\n\nOne judgment call worth flagging: the spec's \"fiscal-year value \u2026 must reference the memberId\" is ambiguous, so I made `getFiscalYear()` derive from the memberId's FY segment (output is identical to the old registration-date derivation for any created owner, since that's what the FY segment is built from).",
